IIRC, heads and tails are not the actual names for them.. if I
remember right the names are obverse and reverse.  Anyway, obverse
refers to the side with the principal design, whatever that may be.  I
*think* the head for american coins is the obverse, but for other
countries, I have no idea.

So in short, heads and tails are just synonyms for obverse and
reverse, but heads would be whatever side the principal design is on. 
Which side is the principal design, I don't, but the official name for
that side is the obverse.

